Z||000000||FIEROMJ||09-24-2001||08:00 PM||||I own an '87 Fiero GT with 92,000 miles on it.  A few monthes back I had to replace the engine on my GT.  The replacement 2.8 has only 2,000 miles on it.  Recently I have been experiencing problems with very erratic idle, engine stalling after start up, a faint ticking coming from the engine compartment, big loss of acceleration, poor gas mileage and a horrible gas odor upon opening the decklid.<BR>I'm assuming I have an exhaust leak.  I have had problems with my exhaust manifolds in the past, and have fixed them by welding every time, but I am not sure if that could be causing so much trouble.  Please give me your suggestions on what you think the problem(s) may be. Thanks. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiero_Freak||09-24-2001||09:45 PM||||   Considering the milage, did you have your catalatic converter replaced?  Sounds like a good place to start.  That might take care of your lack of power.  That's what caused my manifolds to heat up and crack.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIERO1985||09-24-2001||09:48 PM||||Ok, yes the exhust manifolds can casue this problem, are they glowing red? that means there is a vacume leak. Are you getting any codes?<P>Erratic Idle- EGR IAC TPS<BR>Poor Gas- EGR or the O2 sensor<BR>loss of power could also be cause to the possable vacume leak or not recieving fuel there are many different causes for these problems but those are the first things I would check<P>Just my 2 cents<P>Hope you get her runnin good  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Dan<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIERO1985||09-24-2001||09:50 PM||||fiero freak did make a good point that I did not think about check the cat for any clogs or problems that will restrict and cause poor excel bad gas smell gas milage and diffinetly some noises and with that are you experiencing any kacles or back presure?<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIEROMJ||09-24-2001||10:14 PM||||Good idea about checking the cat.  It hasn't been replaced.  I'll have it checked out.  As for the TPS, I had that replaced last September.  I don't know how old the O2 sensor in my car is.  About how long does one of these last?  Same question for the IAC, this part has not been replaced either to my knowledge.  The EGR appears to be in good condition.  All I looked for was a crack in the tube though, I found none.  I checked to see if my manifolds were glowing red and no they weren't.  No kacles either. Thanks for the help so far!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_Freak||09-27-2001||09:15 PM||||   any luck with your problem yet?||||reg||1
